==Latin==

===Etymology===
The accusative singular masculine form of the pronominal stem {{term||na-|lang=la}}; compare the interjection {{term|nē||truly”, “verily”, “really”, “indeed|lang=la}}. Confer with its feminine form {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|nam|lang=la}}, as in {{term|cum|lang=la}}-{{term|quam|lang=la}}, {{term|tum|lang=la}}-{{term|tam|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/num/|lang=la}}

===Adverb===
{{head|la|adverbs}}

# [[now]] ''(only in the phrase, [[etiam]] num)''
# (''in a direct question'') a particle expecting a [[negation]]
#: '''''Num''' Sparta insula est? — Sparta non est insula!''
#:: Sparta isn't an island, is it? — Sparta is not an island!
# (''in an indirect question'') [[whether]]

